Escalated from skilletor#k241. The cpanfile of Skilletor, the Perl port in Getty/skilletor (perl/), requires Text::Nunjucks 0.001. Skilletor's next CPAN release (0.002) cannot install until Text::Nunjucks 0.001 is on CPAN.

What Skilletor uses today (perl/lib/Skilletor/Render.pm, Render/Loader.pm):
- Text::Nunjucks::Environment->new($loader, ...)
- a subclass of Text::Nunjucks::Loader
- Text::Nunjucks::Runtime->None

It does not use the top-level index.js API (configure, render, compile). This is input for k114, not a decision: from Skilletor's side, 0.001 could ship without k20, as long as the POD says Environment is the entry point.

Release blockers already on this board: k24 (pre-release audit of 2026-11-13), k114, k111 (what the tarball ships) and k110 (Path::Tiny runtime vs test). The release happens only on the maintainer's explicit go.
